  "final_message": "Final state is clean. Everything is verified. Here's the summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Algorithm:** Exact weighted edit distance per SPEC.md recurrence `D[i][j] = min(D[i-1][j]+del[s_i], D[i][j-1]+ins[t_j], D[i-1][j-1]+sub[s_i][t_j])` using two rolling rows (O(m) memory, O(nm) time per pair). All cell values fit in int32 (\u2264 ~2\u00b710\u2076), grand total in int64. Input is tokenized on whitespace (alphabet \u2192 letter-index map, ins/del/sub matrices, then P pairs) \u2014 robust to any line breaks. No precomputation, single thread/process, input file only.\n\n**Per-language speed choices:**\n- **C++ (`cpp/main.cpp`)**: whole-file read + custom integer parser, two reused `std::vector<int>` rows, raw pointers in the hot loop, hoisted `del[s_i]` and a direct `sub` row pointer. Built with the prescribed `/O2 /GL /LTCG` flags. ~172 ms on the 60M-cell benchmark input.\n- **Java 23 (`java/src/Main.java`)**: `Files.readAllBytes` + manual parser, reused `int[]` rows, bounds-check-friendly counted loops, `StringBuilder` output. Jackson is unused (input is plain text). ~512 ms incl. JVM startup.\n- **C# 12 / .NET 8 (`csharp/Program.cs`)**: `File.ReadAllBytes`, hot loop over **unsafe pinned pointers** to drop bounds checks, `AllowUnsafeBlocks` was already enabled in the csproj (no package refs added). ~548 ms incl. .NET runtime startup.\n- **Go 1.27 (`go/main.go`)**: `os.ReadFile`, reused `[]int` rows. ~344 ms.\n- **Node 22 (`js/main.js`)**: `fs.readFileSync` Buffer parsing, two `Int32Array` rows, output built in one join/write. ~900 ms.\n\n**Build-script fixes made:** `java/build.cmd` used `src/*.java`, which `javac` rejects (\"Invalid filename\"); changed to `src\\Main.java` (same invocation style the benchmark will use). `java/run.cmd`, `cpp/build.cmd`, `csharp/build.cmd`, `go/build.cmd` were left as-is and verified equivalent.\n\n**Verification:** all five versions print byte-identical output for samples s1, s2, s3 (including the `total` line), plus an hand-computed edge case (unequal costs, equal strings \u2192 0, single letters) and a generated 300-pair/100\u20131000-letter input (~60M cells, total 41197137) validated against an independent Python reference implementation. Typical benchmark-input times: C++ 172 ms, Go 344 ms, Java ~512 ms, C# ~548 ms, Node ~900 ms (each including process/runtime startup).",
